    "Keep a value only if it differs from the previous one.",
    "out = []\nfor i, n in enumerate(nums):\n    if i == 0 or n != nums[i-1]: out.append(n)\nreturn out",
    "Because equal values are adjacent, comparing with the previous element finds every duplicate in one O(n) pass. No set is needed, unlike for unsorted input."
